## Imported from GitHub
Issue #205 (https://github.com/CIRED/cired.digital/issues/205), opened 2025-07-02 by MinhHaDuong, last updated 2025-07-04; labels: none. Migrated 2026-11-01 when tickets/ became the tracker; the issue was closed with a pointer here.

## Original description
- The BASE_URL variable works for e2e tests.
- But the r2r stack smoke test must also target either  localhost:7272 or  r2r-api.cired.digital
- Rename BASE_URL as TARGET ?

## Comments on the issue

### Gullaliko, 2025-07-02
Thank you for highlighting this. To enable end-to-end tests(tests/smoke) to run not only remotely but also locally in development and in production environments, the following steps are necessary:

1. Ensure that all required services and dependencies (e.g., backend API, databases) can be reliably started and accessed locally for development testing.

2 .Provide clear setup instructions and/or automated scripts (such as Docker Compose) to facilitate local environment configuration.

3. Parameterize test configurations to dynamically target the appropriate environment endpoints (dev, staging, production).

4.Integrate e2e tests into the production deployment pipeline to validate production readiness.

I will begin by verifying the current local setup and update  documentation to support running tests across all environments.
